# Festiva: GenAI Celebration & Event Planner

## Stack
Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript (strict) + Tailwind + shadcn/ui + Zod + Vitest + Playwright.
AI: Gemini via @google/genai, called ONLY from server routes in app/api/*.

## Structure
- app/            routes and pages
- app/api/        server routes (plan, refine)
- components/     small, single-purpose UI components
- lib/            schema.ts (Zod), gemini.ts, budget.ts, rate-limit.ts
- tests/          unit tests (Vitest) and e2e (Playwright)
- PROMPTS.md      log of key prompts and how they evolved (update when prompts change)

## Standards
- TypeScript strict mode, no `any`, no dead code, no unused exports.
- Components under ~150 lines; extract hooks/helpers when larger.
- Every AI response is validated with Zod before it reaches the UI.
- Never expose GEMINI_API_KEY to the client. No NEXT_PUBLIC_ for secrets.
- Validate all request bodies with Zod. Add rate limiting to every API route.
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML. Treat AI output as untrusted text.
- Accessibility: labelled inputs, visible focus, keyboard navigation, WCAG AA contrast,
  aria-live for the chat and loading states.
- Always show loading, error, and empty states.
- Add or update tests with every feature (budget math, schema parsing, one e2e flow).
- Run `npm run lint && npm run test` before finishing a task.

## Workflow
Plan first, then implement one small step at a time. Explain what changed after each step.
